<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 0.9 pct in June 1-20 -NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 0.9 pct in June 1-20 -NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money supply rose 1.39 billion zlotys, or 0.9 percent, in the June 1-20 period to 149.65 billion after a 2.4 percent rise in May, preliminary central bank figures show.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 10.2 percent in the January-June 20 period.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		    JUNE 1-20     MAY    JUNE 96</p>
<p>  period pct change			 0.9	  2.4	 1.6</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   149.65     148.26    116.91</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	26.00	25.75     21.53</p>
<p>  National currency		     123.65     122.52     95.38</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    25.98	25.93     22.35</p>
